# Supabase configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values from your Supabase project:
#   Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API
#
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real values. The anon/public key is safe
# to expose in a client app (Row-Level Security protects your data); the
# service_role key must NEVER be put here or in the client.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined into the client bundle at build time. After
# changing them, restart the dev server with `npx expo start -c` to clear cache.

# Note: with Supabase's newer key format the client-safe key is called the
# "publishable" key (sb_publishable_...); it plays the same role as the older
# "anon" key, so it goes in the ANON_KEY variable below.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-publishable-key
